67], "slug": "super-spell-heroes", "summary": "\"Super Spell Heroes is a real-time 1v1 puzzle duel game published by Flaregames and developed by a team of industry veterans (formerly InnoGames, Bigpoint, Goodgame Studios) at Hamburg studio Sviper. \n \nIn Super Spell Heroes, players engage in quickfire battles against fellow wizards using simple colour-matching controls. To win a duel, players match mystical spells to damage their opponent, block against their moves, or quickly replenish their own health. Leaving a trail of fallen wizards in their wake, players will journey through magical realms while unlocking and upgrading new spells. Several playable characters can be discovered and levelled up along the way, from Tierra The Huntress to Lua The Voodoo Priest, each harnessing their own unique spells that enable fresh competitive tactics.\"", "themes": [17], "updated_at": 1670944969, "checksum": "2c8fe273-1735-e5d6-abbf-3ed7128908b9", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 60723, "created_at": 1504860250, "first_release_date": 1419984000, "name": "International Jetpack Conference", "platforms": [82, 13], "release_dates": [186020, 186021], "slug": "international-jetpack-conference", "summary": "Adventure game made in ZZT. Journalist interviews people by repeatedly bumping into them, then solves puzzles.", "updated_at": 1670944980, "checksum": "8d2645e6-448c-5414-91fa-1d80e9854cb9", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 112571, "created_at": 1542879565, "name": "Special Force 2 SEA", "slug": "special-force-2-sea", "updated_at": 1670944988, "checksum": "13bad5fb-c790-4a24-8adf-f1924ed580fd", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 97851, "created_at": 1524580214, "name": "Age of Gladiators II: Death League", "slug": "age-of-gladiators-ii-death-league", "summary": "Age of Gladiators II: Death League is a single-player strategy game set in 3000AD; a violent and unpredictable future where the gladiatorial games have surged in popularity throughout the known galaxy. \n \nHire scouts to scour the planets for potential prospects \u2013 once you have recruited your gladiators through the draft, scouting, missions, trades, or waiver wire acquisitions, you will need to manage their morale and personality while equipping them for battle on the harsh combat environments of various worlds. Recruit support staff, upgrade your headquarters, collect bounties, research technologies, build your headquarters, partake in side missions, and manage the wealth and reputation of your empire as it grows each day. \n \nAs your fighters win battles and increase in level, it will be up to you to decide how to focus their abilities by spending attribute, weapons, and expertise points. Compete, trade, and interact with other in-game owners as you fight through fifty-nine grueling, regular season battles in order to reach the playoffs, vying for the chance to etch your name for all eternity on the coveted Blood League championship trophy. \nBuild your story. Build your empire.", "updated_at": 1670944992, "checksum": "af005683-2257-c892-ce06-7d70b55aa1e8", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 108823, "created_at": 1536223316, "name": "Weave", "slug": "weave", "updated_at": 1670945029, "checksum": "db607d45-da22-5091-701c-4a9b2dea9d62", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 46535, "created_at": 1499632448, "first_release_date": 791596800, "genres": [14], "name": "College Football's National Championship II", "platforms": [29], "release_dates": [98475], "slug": "college-footballs-national-championship-ii", "summary": "It still has the standard set of modes such as Exhibition, Tournament and Season and updated rosters for the top schools of the time, reflecting the 1994 season. There are 32 teams with five added ones to this version (Wisconsin, North Carolina, Colorado State, Oregon and Washington State), however to add these schools five others were taken out that were in the previous game (San Diego State, Pitt, LSU, Arkansas and Houston). It also keeps track of 19 different stats along with authentic offensive and defensive play