jectives, such as destroy a certain amount of enemies or defend certain targets. The planes are mostly modern age such as the A-10 Warthog. The player can choose to use either the plane's machine guns or missiles to bring down enemy targets.", "themes": [1], "updated_at": 1670975201, "checksum": "2a1db653-63b0-027f-1bb1-49798375f1f6", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 32107, "created_at": 1495662120, "first_release_date": 1468368000, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [12, 31, 32], "involved_companies": [74529], "name": "The Sunset", "platforms": [6], "release_dates": [75687], "slug": "the-sunset", "summary": "When a person becomes too lazy to perform his functions, he comes up with all sorts of simplification. \nMankind has invented them - aim to simplify your life. Mechanoids had to perform all kinds of activities. \nAnd at some point completely replace humans in the workspace.But slowly make the perfect workers, the people made a mistake. \nThis mistake cost the lives of more than 80% of the world population, because the mechanoids are out of control - they began to kill everything that moves. \n \nFor the time mechanoids held on our mortal planet, they have changed a lot. Now most of the planet surrounded by rocks. \nFloating in the air dust from the destroyed buildings. The mechanoids themselves become covered with stone chips. \nAnd they began to build their structures, which are called hives. Hives transform the earth into a more useful resource for mechanoid - stone. \nWith which they build their world. \n \nBut not all the people died. So raise all the forces to defeat what we have created!", "themes": [1], "updated_at": 1670975226, "checksum": "2225c2de-5347-7216-bd42-6c157a00228e", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 25335, "created_at": 1477904070, "first_release_date": 1469750400, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [31, 32], "involved_companies": [41276], "name": "Whispers", "platforms": [6], "rating": 40.0, "rating_count": 0, "release_dates": [59873], "slug": "whispers", "summary": "Whispers is a first-person horror game. You play the role as a caretaker of a house out in the country. You have to keep an eye on the house for your friend. The house is located somewhere in a field away from the city. He left instructions for you to follow.", "themes": [1, 19], "total_rating": 40.0, "total_rating_count": 0, "updated_at": 1670975228, "checksum": "82f3c559-021e-aef4-ab1f-6feba4d8a054", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 4288, "created_at": 1390761962, "first_release_date": 788832000, "name": "Seal of the Pharaoh", "platforms": [50], "release_dates": [318186], "slug": "seal-of-the-pharaoh", "summary": "Seal of the Pharaoh is a mix of RPG, puzzle-solving and first-person adventuring.", "updated_at": 1670975239, "checksum": "1448367b-878b-5a5a-bae1-e857036f5f14", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 23730, "created_at": 1473262566, "first_release_date": 1471392000, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [33], "name": "Toxic Bubbles", "platforms": [39], "release_dates": [56293], "slug": "toxic-bubbles", "summary": "A action based bubble popping puzzle game. Interactive swipe based controls and system of levels and chapters make for exciting bubble adventure.", "themes": [1], "updated_at": 1670975240, "checksum": "13e41e2d-6a23-1903-ffcf-3f222b5df1fc", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 27915, "created_at": 1490109038, "involved_companies": [45434], "name": "Lila's Tale", "platforms": [55], "slug": "lilas-tale", "summary": "Immerse yourself in a fantastic and artistic experience, inside a dungeon crawler, crafted for Virtual Reality. Explore the mysteries lying beneath the dungeon, solve chain reaction puzzles and keep Lila safe to find her lost little brother.", "updated_at": 1670975260, "checksum": "a1cd403e-1496-1cd6-a54c-cf299a8c50b5", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 105460, "created_at": 1532026338, "name": "Bound By", "slug": "bound-by", "updated_at": 1670975261, "checksum": "29682209-850e-339e-f4e2-7a8e79d231fb", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 68346, "created_at": 1505941118, "first_release_date": 599529600, "game_modes": [1, 2], "genres": [5, 33], "involved_companies": [54480, 54479], "name": "Future Tank", "platforms": [16], "release_dates": [113618], "slug": "future-tank", "themes": [1, 18], "updated_at": 1670975262, "checksum": "4989110f-9956-3a6e-5df0-c2b4cb1d9915", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 14277, "created_at": 1445788897, "first_release_date": 599529600, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [8], "involved_companies": [27652, 55616], "name": "Australo Piticus Mechanicus", "platforms": [16], "release_dates": [119495], "slug": "australo-piticus-mechanicus", "themes": [17, 18], "updated_at": 1670975263, "checksum": "d9f3bb70-f082-189c-8c33-48ead4032c9a", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 4398, "created_at": 1390774529, "first_release_date": 752457600, "genres": [10], "name": "Metal Fangs", "platforms": [29], "release_dates": [10142], "slug": "metal-fangs", "summary": "Metal Fangs is a game for the Sega Mega Drive by Victor. It was not released outside of Japan. It's an Arcade racing game with top-down perspective in which two teams of four circle a track with the goal of eliminating each other.", "updated_at": 1670975279, "checksum": "3b75e44b-fde0-6660-a99f-6590cd640d59", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 112522, "created_at": 1542878967, "name": "The Moon or Bust!", "slug": "the-moon-or-bust", "updated_at": 1670975280, "checksum": "759eb1df-5583-b5c9-24ff-9b1658d7a7c1", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 112515, "created_at": 1542878710, "name": "Rising Fire", "slug": "rising-fire", "updated_at": 1670975285, "checksum": "ed605a0a-2063-197f-ecb1-812407c4148e", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 6122, "created_at": 1397821936, "first_release_date": 441676800, "name": "Pacar", "platforms": [84], "release_dates": [15558], "slug": "pacar", "summary": "Pacar is an SG-1000 game initially released in 1983. It is essentially a mix between two Namco games; Pac-Man and Rally X. \n \nIt is the sequel to Head-On, which was released a year before Puck-Man. However, Pacar is more-so a clone of Puck-Man than a true Head-On sequel. \n \nThe player controls \"Pacar\", a \"mischievous\" green car through a maze of roads. The objective of the game is to \"delete\" all of the small red \"dots\" scattered around the playfield, building up points for a high score. The joystick allows Pacar to move in the proposed direction, assuming it is possible to do so. Like Pac-Man, Pacar does not stop moving unless it hits a wall, however unlike Pac-Man, it is not possible to rotate 180 degrees on the spot - moving in the opposite direction causes Pacar to reverse, and reversing is significantly slower than driving normally. Ideally the player should plan his or her route to avoid reversing altogether. \n \n1 or 2 allows Pacar to move faster across the board. Driving off the edge of the screen makes Pacar appear at the other side, again similar to Pac-Man. \n \nThe game has Pacar avoid two types of enemy, also depicted as cars. Blue cars spawn from the garage at the centre of the screen and wander around the play area, only following Pacar if it is close by. Red cars spawn randomly on the road behind Pacar, and are much more aggressive with their tactics. Red cars also differ in that if Pacar speeds up, they will also increase their speed. If either car crashes into Pacar under normal conditions, the player loses a life. \n \nUnder certain conditions the game's equivalent of Pac Man's power pellets appear after deleting smaller dots. These give Pacar \"temporary invincibility\" turning it purple in the process, and act as the only form of attack against oppoents. While purple, the player is free to crash into as many cars as he or she likes, and is granted extra points in the process (starting at 200 and doubling for each successive hit, i.e. 200, 400, 800, 1600, 3200 etc.). It will also slow down red cars. Though there are typically fewer enemies on-screen in Pacar than Pac-Man, the fact that blue cars spawn from the garage instantly after being deleted means it is possible to achieve much higher point combos. \n \nThere are only two maps in Pacar, which cycle endlessly until the player dies. The game claims it is \"three dimensional\" as some roads in map 1 act as bridges over other roads. Once both maps are completed the player proceeds to the next \"round\", in which more blue cars are added to the playfield (with the exception of round 4, in which the three \"normal\" blue cars are replaced with one faster blue car. Round 5 will then add a second faster car and so on). \n \nExtra lives are awarded every 10,000 points.", "themes": [1], "updated_at": 1670975291, "checksum": "114583d1-bdc0-6f62-b114-d833a4469e04", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 6138, "created_at": 1397822180, "first_release_date": 412905600, "genres": [5], "name": "Space Slalom", "platforms": [84], "release_dates": [99033], "slug": "space-slalom", "summary": "Space Slalom is a video game developed by Orca and published by Sega for the SG-1000 in 1983. \n \nThough on the surface it appears to be a space-themed vertical shoot-'em-up, there is actually no shooting involved. The player controls a shuttle and must navigate it through a course defined by colored stars, similar to ski slaloms. The player must also avoid obstacles, and will be awarded with extra points depending on on his/her speed across the course. \n \nAt a mere 8kB, the game is one of the smallest SG-1000 games, and was only sold in Japan.", "updated_at": 1670975291, "checksum": "709c2170-3e60-ea9d-fe8e-2e90bb9b4842", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 14634, "created_at": 1448133218, "first_release_date": 631065600, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [15, 33], "involved_companies": [28351], "name": "Day of the Pharaoh", "platforms": [13, 16], "release_dates": [40817, 40818], "slug": "day-of-the-pharaoh", "themes": [22], "updated_at": 1670975303, "checksum": "b5c77cb9-a028-39bd-acfd-877c65c7b82a", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 68347, "created_at": 1505943255, "first_release_date": 599529600, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [33], "involved_companies": [54482], "name": "St