g": "bostilda", "summary": "A.B. Cop is a futuristic 3D racing arcade game released by Sega in 1990.[3] Gameplay is similar to that of Chase H.Q.. \n \nThe player takes on the role of the A.B. (Air Bike) Cop who must chase down and destroy the perpetrators of various crimes (which changes every level) before the time limit expires. A.B Cop introduced an element new to the racing genre: the end-of-level guardian.", "updated_at": 1670976326, "checksum": "1361beb1-7be9-7332-abef-865bc33f40d2", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 133971, "created_at": 1589683053, "genres": [5, 33], "involved_companies": [99172], "name": "Centroid", "platforms": [6], "slug": "centroid", "storyline": "\"Planet Centroid - Mankind's last chance in a dying universe. The cosmos themselves are raining down. Defend it with everything you've got.\"", "summary": "Defend your planet from incoming space debris. Blast asteroids, avoid collisions, use power-ups - and get a high score! This game plays like a twin-stick-shooter with a twist. All movement is \"orbital.\" Your ship moves in an orbit around your planet, as do the enemies. It's a pretty neat spin on the classic space-shooter genre.", "updated_at": 1670976331, "checksum": "00592cdb-13bb-4531-8f73-8fea1b5c52dc", "game_status": 4, "game_type": 0}, {"id": 138954, "created_at": 1600364163, "first_release_date": 1600819200, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [31], "involved_companies": [108481], "name": "Aruna's Adventure", "platforms": [39], "release_dates": [211043], "slug": "arunas-adventure", "storyline": "The player takes control of the blue haired heroine Aruna, who along with her guiding fairy is trying to stop the Dark Lord from infesting the lands with monsters. \nAruna explores the multiple landscapes of the world fighting monsters, finding secrets, entering dungeons and fighting bosses.", "summary": "Aruna\u2019s Adventure takes you on a nostalgic trip back to the early '90s action adventure games. It has a vibrant 8 bit pixel art style and an emphasis