ustomize an invitation using stationery, paints, and stickers, and then save it to your device.\n\u2022 Cupcakes \u2013 Decorate some tasty treats with pinkerrific frosting, sprinkles, and colorful wrappers. Then, serve the cupcakes to Pinkalicious, Peter, and all of their friends!\n\u2022 Music Maker \u2013 Experiment with music and try all the party horns, listening to their different sounds and notes as you pass them out to characters and make your own songs.\n\u2022 Photobooth \u2013 Take a photo, pick a photo from your device, or use a character's photo to decorate and frame at the party. The decorated photo will be saved to the device to view and share with family and friends!\n\u2022 Pi\u00f1ata \u2013 Choose your favorite shape and dunk it in paint and decorations, then break open the pi\u00f1ata to see the treats inside!\n \n\nCREATIVITY & ARTS \n\u2022 Every activity was designed for kids to use art, music and imagination to create a party that is uniquely their own!  \n\u2022 Each location is filled with interactions your child can explore: tapping decorations to change them, moving the characters, and finding little surprises hidden in each party.\n\n\nABOUT PINKALICIOUS & PETERRIFIC\u2122\nBased on the best-selling books by Victoria Kann, Pinkalicious & Peterrific\u2122 is a PBS KIDS series produced by WGBH and Sixteen South that explores the arts, creativity, and self-expression. Anything is possible when you use your imagination!\n \nWatch Pinkalicious & Peterrific\u2122 anytime on the PBS KIDS Video App and find more games and activities at pbskids.org/pinkalicious\n\n\nABOUT PBS KIDS\nPinkalicious Party is part of PBS KIDS\u2019 ongoing commitment to helping kids build the skills they need to succeed in school and in life. PBS KIDS, the number one educational media brand for kids, offers children ages 2-8 the opportunity to explore new ideas and new worlds through television, digital media and community-based programs. PBS KIDS and local stations across the country support the entire ecosystem in which children learn, including their teachers, parents and community.\n\nFor more apps from PBS KIDS, visit pbskids.org/apps.\n\nPRIVACY\nAcross all media platforms, PBS KIDS is committed to creating a safe and secure environment for children and families and being transparent about what information is collected from users. To learn more about PBS KIDS\u2019 privacy policy, visit pbskids.org/privacy.", "total_rating": 70.0, "total_rating_count": 0, "updated_at": 1670982275, "checksum": "f7e4f433-6d26-2ff6-b724-bf2749a799e0", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 13520, "created_at": 1444763758, "first_release_date": 536371200, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [5, 33], "involved_companies": [47386], "name": "Cosmic Shock Absorber", "platforms": [15, 26, 25, 27], "release_dates": [71001, 71000, 70999, 71002], "slug": "cosmic-shock-absorber", "themes": [1, 18], "updated_at": 1670982276, "checksum": "fa5f31b0-dc46-c963-44b6-755e7896fb72", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 54284, "created_at": 1501688852, "name": "Pool House", "slug": "pool-house", "updated_at": 1670982277, "checksum": "06992c0f-dcd2-dd2c-1668-c9574742d16f", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 99708, "created_at": 1524987366, "name": "Destroy the House - Smash Home Interiors", "rating": 41.888824, "rating_count": 0, "slug": "destroy-the-house-smash-home-interiors", "total_rating": 41.888824, "total_rating_count": 0, "updated_at": 1670982277, "checksum": "c557ac1c-0d38-4409-c77f-cb6b03c513b6", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 52692, "created_at": 1501430496, "name": "Recoil: Retrograd", "slug": "recoil-retrograd", "updated_at": 1670982278, "checksum": "03fd3b9c-f742-19d7-8eb2-bbe7b2c41381", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 99265, "created_at": 1524915052, "name": "Kings of Soccer", "slug": "kings-of-soccer", "updated_at": 1670982278, "checksum": "275ab2d6-3025-e04b-6b9f-c959fa032e31", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 93836, "created_at": 1521377975, "name": "Nindash: Skull Valley", "slug": "nindash-skull-valley", "updated