 of 2011, there are no known Mega Drive-compatible Sansan servers. A local two-player version of the game is also included for play. \n \nFor whatever reason, the Mega Drive version did not last very long \u2014 it is one of the rarest and most sought-after Mega Drive games; Sega of Japan's official archive doesn't list it (despite Sansan Co., Ltd. having T-series code T-147) and a ROM was not dumped until February 2011. The Windows PC version of the service continues to this day.", "updated_at": 1670983011, "checksum": "ee930ce3-fd6b-4b4b-482f-5933c056bbbf", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 104560, "created_at": 1530264277, "first_release_date": 1341964800, "involved_companies": [120496], "name": "Absolute RC Simulator", "platforms": [39], "release_dates": [231799], "slug": "absolute-rc-simulator", "updated_at": 1670983011, "checksum": "4c51b0d6-a7f4-0167-36e9-bfe7c6c97cca", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 91074, "created_at": 1521065821, "name": "Alien Story: Games for kids", "slug": "alien-story-games-for-kids", "updated_at": 1670983013, "checksum": "cd2bcdc5-9d89-7341-9b8b-b7a651dd5166", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 38701, "created_at": 1497982215, "name": "Retro Defense", "slug": "retro-defense", "updated_at": 1670983020, "checksum": "562c2011-1fc6-a531-efc8-e0283e4fe942", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 128624, "created_at": 1579429886, "first_release_date": 1388448000, "name": "Atum", "platforms": [82, 6], "release_dates": [185987, 185988], "slug": "atum", "summary": "ATUM pulls the player into a world where the player is the mechanic. It brings a novelty take on the point-and-click gameplay of previous generations and combines it with platformer puzzles. The game toys with the concept of multi-layer gameplay, dipping its layers in mathematical loops and philosophical recurrences. \n \nThe design and the aesthetics are influenced by a manifold of science fiction classics, Blade Runner and Philip K. Dick's story Martian Time Slip among others. \n \nThe game environment, used as narrative device, provides a considerable amount of references and clues that complement the underlying storyline.", "updated_at": 1670983022, "checksum": "5b879cb7-9767-d010-3ad8-f7772b35e723", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 139486, "created_at": 1602273507, "name": "Labyrinths of the World: Changing the Past", "slug": "labyrinths-of-the-world-changing-the-past", "updated_at": 1670983023, "checksum": "eba9322a-333f-6a9d-e24e-5b96c42e9e97", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 87238, "created_at": 1518699375, "name": "Ocean - Find Matching Images", "rating": 50.0, "rating_count": 0, "slug": "ocean-find-matching-images", "total_rating": 50.0, "total_rating_count": 0, "updated_at": 1670983027, "checksum": "5d09928a-a995-0d5c-141a-d11248ceb688", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 113645, "created_at": 1547106473, "game_modes": [1], "genres": [12, 13, 31, 32], "name": "Dodgerman", "slug": "dodgerman", "summary": "Once, when you spent time with your girlfriend \u2026 An incident occurred \u2026 \u201cWhy do you have two toothbrushes?\u201d Another girl forgot one of these here You need some kind of redemption. Try to wiggle out of this dangerous situation! All outcomes of these bloody amorous battles depends on your decisions!", "updated_at": 1670983029, "checksum": "189be3ea-3440-652a-5252-14f538507b74", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 100732, "created_at": 1525687797, "name": "Kill the Plumber World", "slug": "kill-the-plumber-world", "updated_at": 1670983032, "checksum": "22c01d5e-a891-a124-8f32-fdf20550c62c", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 109286, "created_at": 1536684592, "hypes": 1, "involved_companies": [69659], "name": "Untitled Project 1", "slug": "untitled-project-1", "summary": "The first of 3 game projects by the new development studio Too Kyo Games. \nIt is the work of Kazutaka Kodaka, Danganronpa series creator, and Kotaro Uchikoshi, Zero Escape series creator.", "updated_at": 1670983033, "checksum": "aeb98ec3-7007-603e-3292-361e975dfa9d", "game_type": 0}, {"id": 128739, "created_at": 1579555867, "first_release_d